    "created_at": "2022-02-18T23:54:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-18T23:55:06Z",
    "body": "If I understand the changes proposed by @domenic correctly, setting `currentTime` to some !`currentTime` would result in `currentTime` returning the prior `currentTime`, not the clamped value as requested in the WPT issue.\r\n\r\nSo, you'd end up with something like:\r\n\r\n```\r\n> video.currentTime\r\n< 1\r\n> video.duration\r\n< 60\r\n> video.currentTime = 120\r\n< 1\r\n> video.currentTime\r\n< 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd this ends up with weird behavior if you do something like:\r\n\r\n```\r\n> video1.currentTime = video2.currentTime = 120\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhere video1 will get seeded to video2's initial currentTime, not 120, and not 120 clamped to video2's duration.\r\n\r\nAm I misunderstanding the proposal to return `current playback position` if the `seeking` flag is true?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
